<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:41:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico reporters blocked from White House after Trump ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22266906c51caeb3d7daf731cf4708dfd4b1598b3bc8ec3808703124256bffad</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban--a8c3f3f48609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban" /><summary type="html">White House correspondents for CNN, MS NOW and Politico on Saturday were blocked from entering the US president's office and residence a day after President Donald Trump announced he was banning the three media outlets for what he called "fake news" coverage. News organisations and press freedom groups have slammed the move as unconstitutional.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Germany braces for key state elections where far right party AfD seeks another breakthrough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d6fe5f565a68b3edbbd5cf1418f408c6d362cfcb3674addbdf1a9a5ab653e59</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:28:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-braces-for-key-state-elections-where-far-right-party-afd-seeks-another-breakthrough--ced0cb860143.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-braces-for-key-state-elections-where-far-right-party-afd-seeks-another-breakthrough" /><summary type="html">Germany is gearing up for two more pivotal state elections on Sunday: in the capital Berlin and in the largely rural region of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. All eyes are on the far-right AfD, which after recording its best ever result in the recent Saxony-Anhalt elections, is hoping to once again make sweeping gains. The anti-immigration party's surging popularity is proving challenging for Chancellor Friedrich Merz and both elections are expected to further test his leadership. Story by Eliza Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron visits remote French territory in the North America, a first in over a decade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f66e2615c820677849c13b6d2accc944eb8dc9de9941b5e69c65831afecd09c</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:25:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/macron-visits-remote-french-territory-in-the-north-america-a-first-in-over-a-decade--a2f6eb83d168.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/macron-visits-remote-french-territory-in-the-north-america-a-first-in-over-a-decade" /><summary type="html">President Emmanuel Macron embarks on a rare and symbolic visit to a remote French territory in the North Atlantic on Saturday, hosting Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney at a time of growing tensions with Washington. The three-day visit to Saint Pierre and Miquelon, a three-island archipelago of under 6,000 people just off Newfoundland, will be the first by a French president in over a decade. Peter O'Brien tells us more about France's only remaining possession in North America.</summary></entry><entry><title>Black smoke seen near Riyadh amid air raid alerts in Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a26ba76d5fd691c0e0a9bf3789cbb6f826e1af93a4eeb5c306d10fe538b0fc0</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:16:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia--6a862c3c701b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">⁠Flames and plumes of smoke ‌were ⁠seen ‌rising near ⁠Riyadh airport this afternoon with flights cancelled and delayed. This as fighting between Saudi-backed government forces and Iran-backed Houthi rebels has killed 48 people in recent hours. The rebels staged a lightning offensive this month, seizing swathes of territory in Yemen and launching a barrage of missiles and drones toward Saudi Arabia. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Jamie Smith-Maillet.</summary></entry><entry><title>As petrol prices rise, France turns to bioethanol – a cheaper fuel alternative</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e4e6228c9d73755a94a3c8202f1d8074149153c5581b784339deb11bdbc6656</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T14:35:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-as-petrol-prices-rise-france-turns-to-bioethanol-_-a-cheaper-fuel-alternative--ca5bda86ae78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-as-petrol-prices-rise-france-turns-to-bioethanol-%E2%80%93-a-cheaper-fuel-alternative" /><summary type="html">With the prices of fuel continuously escalating, more and more drivers have been switching to bioethanol in France. It's cheaper to produce and currently costs around 95 cents per liter. Details by Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>China is now Rwanda’s biggest export market – now comes the hard part</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81940b123c6a6ccd7c769c224af401cc2fe81e1c9552285c9b71dba7b83da8c8</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:30:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-china-is-now-rwanda-s-biggest-export-market-_-now-comes-the-hard-part--a374c5f30bd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-china-is-now-rwanda-s-biggest-export-market-%E2%80%93-now-comes-the-hard-part" /><summary type="html">In the first quarter of 2026, China became the leading destination for Rwandan exports, accounting for 26% of the total, compared with less than 5% just one year earlier. A spectacular shift, driven by the removal of Chinese tariffs on almost all Rwandan products. But on the ground, access to this market of 1.4 billion consumers depends less on tariffs than on meeting sanitary standards. Report by Aurore Bayoud.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's Macron hosts Canadian PM Carney amid US tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2063702b3fc1bcb02b97ccb713549cfba447be90dcc3c7a1505463222d3456f1</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:25:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-hosts-canadian-pm-carney-amid-us-tensions--fd243e3b2664.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-hosts-canadian-pm-carney-amid-us-tensions" /><summary type="html">President Emmanuel Macron embarks on a rare and symbolic visit to a remote French territory in the North Atlantic on Saturday, hosting Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney at a time of growing tensions with Washington. This comes after European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen proposed making Canada the EU’s first associate member. Analysis by Guillaume Lavoie, associate member of the Raoul-Dandurand chair in strategic and diplomatic studies.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin says Europe is 'preparing for war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4daa31975a67aeadf4e5a173c8f6ac3636715214a93f1b4c64f49c94c59d132</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:04:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/putin-says-europe-is-preparing-for-war--d7dfde1b7973.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/putin-says-europe-is-preparing-for-war" /><summary type="html">As the West continues to denounce Russian aggression in Ukraine and to support Kyiv with a host of economic and military measures, Russian President Vladimir Putin says that Nato is expanding its reach and influence with the intention of preparing for war with Russia. Analysis by Dr Alexander Titov, lecturer in Modern European History at Queen's University Belfast in the UK.</summary></entry><entry><title>Millions without power in Cuba as electrical grid collapses again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10e42f3bc0ec7710bda4b6972ae742b1242e8f732eab93b842019e53a2f521e4</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:01:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again--8d09cc02680d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again" /><summary type="html">Cuba was plunged into its seventh massive blackout of the year on Friday. The island of over nine million people endures constant power cuts due to the poor state of its aging thermoelectric plants – but the situation has worsened significantly since January, when Washington imposed a de facto energy blockade on the island. Story by Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Smoke, flames seen near Riyadh airport, ‘major’ flight disruptions reported</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca85cc3d8cc6f12626c272803b352b7f6bb567ee77a10cb646230fee5b6f6b63</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T12:53:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported--d192137a4871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported" /><summary type="html">A plume of smoke and flames rose near Riyadh's main international airport on Saturday and residents reported hearing loud booms hours after Saudi authorities issued the first alert for the country's capital since the latest escalation with Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels. An Aramco fuel tank near the airport was reportedly on fire, according to a journalist in Riyadh.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: 'NAZA' documentary sparks political storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1335afea5284c5549e639937fe6e2300fa8536de4f69638524b8c4eb612501f0</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:40:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T12:41:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm--19a457356dcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm" /><summary type="html">The documentary film 'NAZA', and its co-directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, are at the centre of a controversy in Israel.The film, which won an award at the Venice Film Festival, features anonymous Israeli sources accusing the military of intentionally killing numerous civilians in Gaza.Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Wednesday that he intended to "strip of their citizenship" those who "defame" the Israeli army.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tunisia’s booming boat industry: From pleasure craft to luxury yachts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a9f6f0820dd39d7010a58489fdd64002a100f1ba371bdef594f15a5a3babc30</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T12:40:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tunisia-s-booming-boat-industry-from-pleasure-craft-to-luxury-yachts--be09a0ac3726.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tunisia-s-booming-boat-industry-from-pleasure-craft-to-luxury-yachts" /><summary type="html">In Tunisia, the summer is ending, but the boating season is still in swing. The boating industry has been quietly growing, despite an overall sluggish economy. Since the sector was reorganized through a trade association in 2024, there have been numerous foreign factories set up and Tunisia has become a hub for boat construction – from pleasure crafts to sophisticated yachts. Report by Lilia Blaise and Fadil Aliriza.</summary></entry><entry><title>37 die in Nigerian custody: Reports blame overcrowding, government disputes claim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64228e5e2f427665bd3d70ba0ebf35213285d5c6bae2732325401133c35d5951</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:26:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/37-die-in-nigerian-custody-reports-blame-overcrowding-government-disputes-claim--2875a91ef8ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/37-die-in-nigerian-custody-reports-blame-overcrowding-government-disputes-claim" /><summary type="html">Authorities in north-central Nigeria are investigating the deaths of 37 people while they were in custody for illegal mining. Officials say the detainees died at a detention facility in Niger state, with the Nigerian Security and Civil Defence Corps pointing to a possible disease outbreak. However, some reports suggest overcrowding and poor ventilation may have contributed to the deaths. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent Sam Olukoya.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian children learn ancient warrior skills amid modern war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b396f765c7ed98c97a02fc1645bb625cd0cd6cb67a580a751a7c8d360810b1b3</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:21:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-children-learn-ancient-warrior-skills-amid-modern-war--fde9fce1fd13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-children-learn-ancient-warrior-skills-amid-modern-war" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian children are learning the skills of 17th-century Cossack warriors – the communities that played a central role in Ukraine history, known for their military skills and horsemanship. But for these students, it is more than a history lesson. It is a chance to escape the reality of growing up during war. Story by Charlotte Lam.</summary></entry><entry><title>New France football boss Zidane names first squad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74f954514ec36503d6a7906bd8bc5977980adc40383a3960e7f9236ed9154023</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:20:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/new-france-football-boss-zidane-names-first-squad--14a06c121214.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/new-france-football-boss-zidane-names-first-squad" /><summary type="html">Football legend Zinedine Zidane says that Kylian Mbappe will be his France captain. Zidane named his first squad since being appointed head coach of France's national football team. His first matches in charge will be against Turkey and Belgium. Details by Nick Rushworth.</summary></entry><entry><title>Suspected alcohol poisoning in Nigeria's Ondo State kills at least 49 people</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18d4412a795ea95800ecc1f78880506e51ea641cf0d2a0e3832da6d7f0888284</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/suspected-alcohol-poisoning-in-nigeria-s-ondo-state-kills-at-least-49-people--5aaebcf6dccb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/suspected-alcohol-poisoning-in-nigeria-s-ondo-state-kills-at-least-49-people" /><summary type="html">In Nigeria's Ondo state, at least 49 people have died and 100 others injured after drinking alcohol suspected to contain methanol. Local authorities say 'Monkey Shoulder', a locally brewed herbal drink with high alcohol content is believed to have been the source of the poisoning, but investigations are still ongoing. State police have announced the arrest of 15 people in connection with the incident. Story by Clemence Waller.</summary></entry><entry><title>Did Trump really obtain 'permanent control' over Greenland?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9a0b5c4c02ded054aad333a12cd8676075ada61a54c4bb1f69ca7a4baf73bd4</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:07:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/did-trump-really-obtain-permanent-control-over-greenland--a125835d55d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/did-trump-really-obtain-permanent-control-over-greenland" /><summary type="html">Danish Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen has described a deal for the US to develop a significant military presence on Greenland, as 'a good agreement'. US President Donald Trump announced the deal on Friday, after he spent months seeking to acquire Greenland, citing threats from Russia and China, and even raised the possibility of military action. Story by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump claims son repaid Russian oligarch who funded wedding festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57072b231a59045925b9867a18e7577f323caba71e7295c55a9898db2b4fce5d</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities--ec19dbba0a0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that his eldest son had repaid a Kremlin-linked Russian businessman who funded two days of lavish wedding celebrations in the Bahamas, after the gift raised questions over foreign influence and ethics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Germany cuts energy tax to lower petrol prices as Merz faces state key elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3647132a6c6cf2edb63464a08e3135c9458309c9eb69b94dccc9f14c044ce883</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:05:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-germany-cuts-energy-tax-to-lower-soaring-petrol-prices--8471e3f9a878.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-germany-cuts-energy-tax-to-lower-soaring-petrol-prices" /><summary type="html">Germany will cut taxes on gasoline and diesel by about 17 cents a litre from October, the government said Friday. The move comes ahead of state elections in the capital Berlin and the northeastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania where Chancellor Friedrich Merz's conservative Christian Democrats are expected to be soundly defeated.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Japan under pressure amid accommodation woes as Asian Games kick off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1759477d8b049739e78e24c0013895ba8a3afe004dc88ae656470ba8c879ce</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:02:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/japan-under-pressure-amid-accommodation-woes-as-asian-games-kick-off--c800f315db92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/japan-under-pressure-amid-accommodation-woes-as-asian-games-kick-off" /><summary type="html">It’s the world's biggest sporting event, held every four years – the 20th edition of Asian games is starting in Japan. Organisers came under pressure even before competition began… as thousands more athletes and officials registered to take part than initially expected. Story by Charlotte Lam.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ebola outbreak reaches new areas in Democratic Republic of Congo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39890586bb03cbd3b20cfaba7aaa892a28649f26822dbc9d6874e70b1a3105d9</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:59:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ebola-outbreak-reaches-new-areas-in-democratic-republic-of-congo--c0ca8e99988f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ebola-outbreak-reaches-new-areas-in-democratic-republic-of-congo" /><summary type="html">In the Democratic Republic of Congo, the government claims that the Ebola outbreak has changed course, with cases trending downwards in hotspots. But that interpretation is being met with pushback from experts and health responders, who say the outbreak remains as bad as ever. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent Emmet Livingstone.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's police launch operation to clear migrants off Ceuta beach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4acbd54e21389e6fbc2de72e390a27159c9887794f2a90694a46c1c47dc7933f</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:57:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-police-launch-operation-to-clear-migrants-off-ceuta-beach--69bde6533cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-police-launch-operation-to-clear-migrants-off-ceuta-beach" /><summary type="html">Police on Friday moved hundreds of migrants from the beaches of Ceuta to a temporary camp in the Spanish enclave's port area. The police operation takes place weeks after a record influx of people into Spain's North African tiny territory. During the transfer, the police struggled to contain crowds jostling to get a place at the new tented site. The policing takes place with the issue of migration centre stage in Spain's political debate. Details by Nicholas Rushworth.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s Macron warns of Russian ‘hybrid’ attacks, seeks to step up energy defence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f75df3cbcd5a926068cb7bd41c39a56fa3332456cf9ab693da387af1cf05f8</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:52:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-warns-of-russian-hybrid-attacks-seeks-to-step-up-energy-defence--04c7e0a32971.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-warns-of-russian-hybrid-attacks-seeks-to-step-up-energy-defence" /><summary type="html">Just months before France's presidential election, rising fuel costs due to the wars in Iran and Ukraine have pushed the nation to the verge of crisis. In an attempt to address public anger and energy threats, French President Emmanuel Macron gathered the nation's major party presidential candidates at the presidential palace. But the main takeaway from this meeting was perhaps Macron's warning about Russian "hybrid attacks"... what exactly does he mean and how serious is the threat? Details and analysis by Richard Werly, France and Europe correspondent for Blick.</summary></entry><entry><title>More than 112,000 displaced in Yemen as Houthis seize more ground</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:980225fadbf8a11467a28cbebaed4ab781b9fd7505277aa4e62244237b29b46e</id><updated>2026-09-19T18:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:57:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground--fdb60ca50a35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground" /><summary type="html">Pro-Houthi demonstrations erupted in Yemen after Saudi Arabia accused the military group of targeting the Muslim holy site of Mecca. Story by Elitsa Gadeva.</summary></entry></feed>
